IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa15-nouns`
IMPORT `coa15-ch1`
IMPORT `coa15-ch4`

-- coa15-ch5.l4: Part 18, Chapter 5 (Redemption or purchase by private company out of capital), ss 709 to 723
-- (lines 9320-9522 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). Layer 1: the law, objectively, with no seat. It imports coa15-ch1.l4 (the statement-of-capital
-- check of s 663(3)) and coa15-ch4.l4 (the voting-rights rules of s 695, which s 717 repeats). Reading a result: as in coa15-ch1.l4.
--
-- Periods in this Chapter: "within the week immediately following the date" is the seven days after that date; "five weeks after" is 35 days
-- after; "seven weeks after" is 49 days after; "within 15 days after" is the 15 days after; "not more than 15 days before" is up to 15 days before.
-- `AFTER` is rejected by the stable binary, so where a lower edge matters (ss 716(2), 719, 723) the decision function holds both edges and the
-- regulative rule holds the closing edge (NOTES.md, "What the stable binary does not accept").

DECLARE `s 714(1) act in Chapter 5` IS ONE OF
    `s 714(1) make a statement in accordance with section 714`
    `s 719(1) cause to be published in the Gazette a notice of the proposed payment`
    `s 719(2) cause to be published in an appropriate national newspaper, or give to each creditor in writing, a notice of the proposed payment`
    `s 719(4) deliver to the registrar a copy of the directors' statement and auditor's report`
    `s 720(3) give notice to the registrar of the place at which the statement and report are kept available for inspection and of any change in that place`
    `s 720B(1) deliver to the registrar a copy of the solvency statement, a copy of the resolution and a statement of capital`
    `s 720B(3) register the documents delivered to him`
    `s 720B(5) deliver to the registrar a statement by the directors confirming the solvency statement`
    `s 721(1) apply to the court for the cancellation of the resolution`
    `s 721(4) make an order either cancelling or confirming the resolution`
    `s 722(1) give notice to the registrar of the application`
    `s 722(2) give notice to the registrar of the notice of the application`
    `s 722(3) deliver to the registrar a copy of the court's order`
    `s 723(1) make the payment out of capital`

-- ---- s 709: power of private limited company to redeem or purchase own shares out of capital --------------

-- src:9323 | (1) A private limited company may in accordance with this Chapter, but subject to any restriction or prohibition in the company's articles, make a payment in respect of the redemption or purchase of its own shares otherwise than out of distributable profits or the proceeds of a fresh issue of shares.
@ref s 709(1) A private limited company may in accordance with this Chapter, subject to any restriction or prohibition in its articles, make a payment out of capital for the redemption or purchase of its own shares (src:9323-9323)
GIVEN `the company is a private limited company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is in accordance with Chapter 5` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company's articles restrict or prohibit the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 709(1) the private limited company may make the payment out of capital` MEANS
    -- fork F-grant-709-1: "may ... make a payment out of capital, ... subject to any restriction or prohibition in the company's articles" is a grant or a power; where its gate fails the answer is NOTHING; the other reading answers JUST FALSE (a failed "if" read as the text's own no); the articles-restrict branch is the one that flips
    IF (NOT `the company is a private limited company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A private limited company may in accordance with this Chapter"
    ELSE IF `the company's articles restrict or prohibit the payment`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "but subject to any restriction or prohibition in the company's articles": what the articles say is outside the text
         ELSE CONSIDER `the payment is in accordance with Chapter 5`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may in accordance with this Chapter"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the payment is in accordance with Chapter 5 is ss 710 to 723, answered by the caller

-- src:9324 | (2) References below in this Chapter to payment out of capital are to any payment so made, whether or not it would be regarded apart from this section as a payment out of capital.
@ref s 709(2) References in this Chapter to payment out of capital are to any payment so made, whether or not it would be regarded apart from this section as a payment out of capital (src:9324-9324)
GIVEN `the payment is a payment in respect of the redemption or purchase of its own shares otherwise than out of distributable profits or the proceeds of a fresh issue of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment would be regarded apart from section 709 as a payment out of capital` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 709(2) the payment is a payment out of capital for the purposes of this Chapter` MEANS
    IF `the payment is a payment in respect of the redemption or purchase of its own shares otherwise than out of distributable profits or the proceeds of a fresh issue of shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- whether or not `the payment would be regarded apart from section 709 as a payment out of capital`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to any payment so made"

-- src:9325 | (3) This Chapter is subject to section 692(1ZA) (purchase of own shares up to annual limit).
@ref s 709(3) This Chapter is subject to section 692(1ZA) (purchase of own shares up to annual limit) (src:9325-9325)
GIVEN `the payment is made out of capital in accordance with section 692(1ZA)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 709(3) the requirements of Chapter 5 are displaced by section 692(1ZA)` MEANS
    IF `the payment is made out of capital in accordance with section 692(1ZA)`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- this Chapter is subject to section 692(1ZA): a payment out of capital made as section 692(1ZA) allows does not have to follow this Chapter (fork F-signpost)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This Chapter is subject to section 692(1ZA)": the text displaces the Chapter only for a payment made under that subsection

-- ---- ss 710 to 712: the permissible capital payment and the available profits -------------------------------------

-- src:9328 | (1) The payment that may, in accordance with this Chapter, be made by a company out of capital in respect of the redemption or purchase of its own shares is such amount as, after applying for that purpose—
-- src:9329 | (a) any available profits of the company, and
-- src:9330 | (b) the proceeds of any fresh issue of shares made for the purposes of the redemption or purchase,
-- src:9331 | is required to meet the price of redemption or purchase.
-- src:9332 | (2) That is referred to below in this Chapter as “the permissible capital payment” for the shares.
@ref s 710(1) The permissible capital payment is the amount required to meet the price after applying any available profits and the proceeds of any fresh issue (src:9328-9332)
GIVEN `the price of the redemption or purchase` IS A NUMBER
      `the available profits of the company` IS A NUMBER
      `the proceeds of any fresh issue of shares made for the purposes of the redemption or purchase` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 710(1) the permissible capital payment` MEANS
    -- a company with no available profits (an amount below nought) applies none: fork F-permissible
    IF `the price of the redemption or purchase`
         GREATER THAN ((IF `the available profits of the company` GREATER THAN 0 THEN `the available profits of the company` ELSE 0)
                       PLUS `the proceeds of any fresh issue of shares made for the purposes of the redemption or purchase`)
    THEN `the price of the redemption or purchase`
           MINUS (IF `the available profits of the company` GREATER THAN 0 THEN `the available profits of the company` ELSE 0)
           MINUS `the proceeds of any fresh issue of shares made for the purposes of the redemption or purchase`
    ELSE 0

DECLARE `s 712(3) kind of payment` IS ONE OF
    `s 712(3)(a) a distribution lawfully made by the company`
    `s 712(4)(a) financial assistance lawfully given out of distributable profits in accordance with Chapter 2`
    `s 712(4)(b) a payment lawfully made out of distributable profits in respect of the purchase by the company of shares in the company`
    `s 712(4)(c) a payment of a description specified in section 705 lawfully made by the company`
    `s 712(4) another kind of payment`

DECLARE `s 712(3) payment` HAS
    `s 712(3) kind of payment` IS A `s 712(3) kind of payment`
    `s 712(3) amount of the payment` IS A NUMBER
    `s 712(3) date of the payment` IS A DATE
    `s 712(3) the payment was lawfully made by the company out of distributable profits` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:9348 | (4) For this purpose “other relevant payment lawfully made” includes—
-- src:9349 | (a) financial assistance lawfully given out of distributable profits in accordance with Chapter 2,
-- src:9350 | (b) payments lawfully made out of distributable profits in respect of the purchase by the company of any shares in the company, and
-- src:9351 | (c) payments of any description specified in section 705 (payments other than purchase price to be made out of distributable profits) lawfully made by the company.
@ref s 712(4) "Other relevant payment lawfully made" includes financial assistance, purchase payments and section 705 payments (src:9348-9351)
GIVEN payment IS A `s 712(3) payment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 712(4) the payment is an other relevant payment lawfully made` MEANS
    CONSIDER payment's `s 712(3) kind of payment`
    WHEN `s 712(3)(a) a distribution lawfully made by the company` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): a distribution is the other limb of subsection (3), "(a) any distribution lawfully made by the company, and (b) any other relevant payment"
    WHEN `s 712(4) another kind of payment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“other relevant payment lawfully made” includes—": the list is not closed
    OTHERWISE
        IF payment's `s 712(3) the payment was lawfully made by the company out of distributable profits`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "financial assistance lawfully given out of distributable profits", "payments lawfully made out of distributable profits", "lawfully made by the company"

-- src:9344 | (3) Second, reduce the amount so determined by the amount of—
-- src:9345 | (a) any distribution lawfully made by the company, and
-- src:9346 | (b) any other relevant payment lawfully made by the company out of distributable profits,
-- src:9347 | after the date of the relevant accounts and before the end of the relevant period.
@ref s 712(3) Reduce the amount determined by any distribution and any other relevant payment lawfully made after the date of the relevant accounts and before the end of the relevant period (src:9344-9347)
GIVEN `the amount determined under subsection (2)` IS A NUMBER
      `the date of the relevant accounts` IS A DATE
      `the end of the relevant period` IS A DATE
      payments IS A LIST OF `s 712(3) payment`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 712(3) the amount after the reduction` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN p YIELD (`s 712(4) the payment is an other relevant payment lawfully made` p) EQUALS NOTHING
                          AND p's `s 712(3) date of the payment` GREATER THAN `the date of the relevant accounts`
                          AND p's `s 712(3) date of the payment` LESS THAN `the end of the relevant period`) payments
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): a payment of a kind the text does not decide is an "other relevant payment" or not
    ELSE JUST (`the amount determined under subsection (2)`
               MINUS sum (map (GIVEN p YIELD p's `s 712(3) amount of the payment`)
                              (filter (GIVEN p YIELD p's `s 712(3) the payment was lawfully made by the company out of distributable profits`
                                                      AND p's `s 712(3) date of the payment` GREATER THAN `the date of the relevant accounts`
                                                      AND p's `s 712(3) date of the payment` LESS THAN `the end of the relevant period`
                                                      AND ((`s 712(4) the payment is an other relevant payment lawfully made` p) EQUALS JUST TRUE
                                                           OR p's `s 712(3) kind of payment` EQUALS `s 712(3)(a) a distribution lawfully made by the company`))
                                      payments)))

-- The text names the items (profits, losses, assets and liabilities; provisions of the kinds specified under section 396 or, for IAS accounts, of any kind;
-- share capital and reserves, including undistributable reserves) but gives no formula: the arithmetic is Part 23's (sections 830 to 836, coa18).
-- The caller states the profits so determined, and `s 396` supplies the provisions of the first kind. NOTHING-kind (points outside the text).
-- src:9337 | (1) The available profits of the company are determined as follows.
-- src:9338 | (2) First, determine the profits of the company by reference to the following items as stated in the relevant accounts—
-- src:9339 | (a) profits, losses, assets and liabilities,
-- src:9340 | (b) provisions of the following kinds—
-- src:9341 | (i) where the relevant accounts are Companies Act accounts, provisions of a kind specified for the purposes of this subsection by regulations under section 396;
-- src:9342 | (ii) where the relevant accounts are IAS accounts, provisions of any kind;
-- src:9343 | (c) share capital and reserves (including undistributable reserves).
@ref s 712(2) First, determine the profits by reference to the items stated in the relevant accounts (src:9337-9343)
GIVEN `the profits of the company determined by reference to the items stated in the relevant accounts` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 712(2) the profits of the company before the reductions` MEANS `the profits of the company determined by reference to the items stated in the relevant accounts`

-- src:9352 | (5) The resulting figure is the amount of available profits.
@ref s 712(5) The resulting figure is the amount of available profits (src:9352-9352)
GIVEN `the amount after the reduction under subsection (3)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 712(5) the amount of the available profits` MEANS `the amount after the reduction under subsection (3)`

-- src:9334 | (1) For the purposes of this Chapter the available profits of the company, in relation to the redemption or purchase of any shares, are the profits of the company that are available for distribution (within the meaning of Part 23).
-- src:9335 | (2) But the question whether a company has any profits so available, and the amount of any such profits, shall be determined in accordance with section 712 instead of in accordance with sections 836 to 842 in that Part.
@ref s 711 Available profits: the profits available for distribution, determined under section 712 instead of sections 836 to 842 (src:9334-9335)
GIVEN `the profits of the company determined by reference to the items stated in the relevant accounts` IS A NUMBER
      `the date of the relevant accounts` IS A DATE
      `the end of the relevant period` IS A DATE
      payments IS A LIST OF `s 712(3) payment`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 711(2) the available profits of the company for the purposes of Chapter 5` MEANS
    -- the amount that sections 836 to 842 would give is not used: "shall be determined in accordance with section 712 instead of in accordance with sections 836 to 842"
    `s 712(5) the amount of the available profits`
        (`s 712(3) the amount after the reduction`
            (`s 712(2) the profits of the company before the reductions` `the profits of the company determined by reference to the items stated in the relevant accounts`)
            `the date of the relevant accounts` `the end of the relevant period` payments)

-- src:9356 | (7) In this section “the relevant period” means the period of three months ending with the date on which the solvency statement is made in accordance with section 720A or the directors' statement is made in accordance with section 714.
@ref s 712(7) "The relevant period" means the period of three months ending with the date on which the solvency statement or the directors' statement is made (src:9356-9356)
GIVEN `the date on which the solvency statement is made in accordance with section 720A or the directors' statement is made in accordance with section 714` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 712(7) the first day of the relevant period` MEANS (`add months` `the date on which the solvency statement is made in accordance with section 720A or the directors' statement is made in accordance with section 714` (0 MINUS 3)) PLUS 1
-- fork F-period-start: "the period of three months ending with the date" is read as beginning the day after the date three months earlier; the other reading begins on that earlier date

-- src:9353 | (6) For the purposes of this section “the relevant accounts” are any accounts that—
-- src:9354 | (a) are prepared as at a date within the relevant period, and
-- src:9355 | (b) are such as to enable a reasonable judgment to be made as to the amounts of the items mentioned in subsection (2).
@ref s 712(6) "The relevant accounts" are accounts prepared as at a date within the relevant period that enable a reasonable judgment to be made (src:9353-9355)
GIVEN `the date as at which the accounts are prepared` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the relevant period` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the solvency statement or the directors' statement is made` IS A DATE
      `the accounts enable a reasonable judgment to be made as to the amounts of the items mentioned in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 712(6) the accounts are the relevant accounts` MEANS
    IF `the date as at which the accounts are prepared` AT LEAST `the first day of the relevant period`
       AND `the date as at which the accounts are prepared` AT MOST `the date on which the solvency statement or the directors' statement is made`
       AND `the accounts enable a reasonable judgment to be made as to the amounts of the items mentioned in subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“the relevant accounts” are any accounts that— (a) are prepared as at a date within the relevant period, and (b) are such as to enable a reasonable judgment to be made as to the amounts of the items mentioned in subsection (2)"

-- ---- s 713: requirements for payment out of capital -----------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9359 | (1) A payment out of capital by a private company for the redemption or purchase of its own shares is not lawful unless the requirements of the following sections are met—
-- src:9360 | section 714 (directors' statement and auditor's report);
-- src:9361 | section 716 (approval by special resolution);
-- src:9362 | section 719 (public notice of proposed payment);
-- src:9363 | section 720 (directors' statement and auditor's report to be available for inspection).
@ref s 713(1) A payment out of capital by a private company is not lawful unless the requirements of sections 714, 716, 719 and 720 are met (src:9359-9363)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements of section 714 are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the requirements of section 716 are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the requirements of section 719 are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the requirements of section 720 are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 713(1) the payment out of capital is not lawful` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a private company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A payment out of capital by a private company"
    ELSE IF (`the requirements of section 714 are met` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`the requirements of section 716 are met` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
            OR (`the requirements of section 719 are met` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (`the requirements of section 720 are met` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF (`the requirements of section 714 are met` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the requirements of section 716 are met` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
                 AND (`the requirements of section 719 are met` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the requirements of section 720 are met` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not lawful unless the requirements of the following sections are met"
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether a requirement is met is not known

-- src:9364 | (2) This is subject to section 720A and to any order of the court under section 721 (power of court to extend period for compliance on application by persons objecting to payment).
@ref s 713(2) This is subject to section 720A and to any order of the court under section 721 (src:9364-9364)
GIVEN `s 720A(1) section 713(1) does not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 713(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the payment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 720A(1) section 713(1) does not apply`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This is subject to section 720A and to any order of the court under section 721": what an order under section 721 does is subsection 721(5), which alters dates and periods

-- ---- s 714: directors' statement and auditor's report ----------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 714(1) directors' statement` HAS
    `s 714(1) the amount of the permissible capital payment the statement specifies` IS A NUMBER
    `s 714(3) the statement says the directors made full inquiry into the affairs and prospects of the company and formed the opinion` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 714(3)(a) the statement says the opinion is that, as regards its initial situation immediately following the date on which the payment out of capital is proposed to be made, there will be no grounds on which the company could then be found unable to pay its debts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 714(3)(b) the statement says the opinion is that, as regards its prospects for the year immediately following that date, the company will be able to continue to carry on business as a going concern throughout that year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 714(4) in forming their opinion under subsection (3)(a) the directors took into account all of the company's liabilities (including any contingent or prospective liabilities)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 714(5) the statement is in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 714(5) the statement contains the prescribed information with respect to the nature of the company's business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 714(6) a report addressed to the directors by the company's auditor is annexed to the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 714(6)(a) the report states that the auditor has inquired into the company's state of affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 714(6)(b) the report states that the amount specified as the permissible capital payment is in his view properly determined in accordance with sections 710 to 712` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 714(6)(c) the report states that he is not aware of anything to indicate that the opinion expressed by the directors as to any of the matters mentioned in subsection (3) is unreasonable in all the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:9366 | (1) The company's directors must make a statement in accordance with this section.
-- src:9367 | (2) The statement must specify the amount of the permissible capital payment for the shares in question.
@ref s 714(2) The statement must specify the amount of the permissible capital payment for the shares in question (src:9366-9367)
GIVEN statement IS A `s 714(1) directors' statement`
      `the permissible capital payment, as section 710 works it out` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 714(2) the statement specifies the amount of the permissible capital payment` MEANS
    IF statement's `s 714(1) the amount of the permissible capital payment the statement specifies` EQUALS `the permissible capital payment, as section 710 works it out`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The statement must specify the amount of the permissible capital payment for the shares in question." (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)

-- src:9368 | (3) It must state that, having made full inquiry into the affairs and prospects of the company, the directors have formed the opinion—
-- src:9369 | (a) as regards its initial situation immediately following the date on which the payment out of capital is proposed to be made, that there will be no grounds on which the company could then be found unable to pay its debts, and
-- src:9370 | (b) as regards its prospects for the year immediately following that date, that having regard to—
-- src:9371 | (i) their intentions with respect to the management of the company's business during that year, and
-- src:9372 | (ii) the amount and character of the financial resources that will in their view be available to the company during that year,
-- src:9373 | the company will be able to continue to carry on business as a going concern (and will accordingly be able to pay its debts as they fall due) throughout that year.
@ref s 714(3) The statement must state that, having made full inquiry, the directors have formed the opinion as to the initial situation and the prospects for the year (src:9368-9373)
GIVEN statement IS A `s 714(1) directors' statement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 714(3) the statement states what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF statement's `s 714(3) the statement says the directors made full inquiry into the affairs and prospects of the company and formed the opinion`
       AND statement's `s 714(3)(a) the statement says the opinion is that, as regards its initial situation immediately following the date on which the payment out of capital is proposed to be made, there will be no grounds on which the company could then be found unable to pay its debts`
       AND statement's `s 714(3)(b) the statement says the opinion is that, as regards its prospects for the year immediately following that date, the company will be able to continue to carry on business as a going concern throughout that year`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It must state that, having made full inquiry into the affairs and prospects of the company, the directors have formed the opinion— (a) ..., and (b) ..." (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)

-- src:9374 | (4) In forming their opinion for the purposes of subsection (3)(a), the directors must take into account all of the company's liabilities (including any contingent or prospective liabilities).
@ref s 714(4) In forming their opinion for the purposes of subsection (3)(a), the directors must take into account all of the company's liabilities (src:9374-9374)
GIVEN statement IS A `s 714(1) directors' statement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 714(4) the directors took into account the liabilities the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF statement's `s 714(4) in forming their opinion under subsection (3)(a) the directors took into account all of the company's liabilities (including any contingent or prospective liabilities)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the directors must take into account all of the company's liabilities (including any contingent or prospective liabilities)" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)

-- src:9375 | (5) The directors' statement must be in the prescribed form and must contain such information with respect to the nature of the company's business as may be prescribed.
@ref s 714(5) The directors' statement must be in the prescribed form and contain the prescribed information (src:9375-9375)
GIVEN statement IS A `s 714(1) directors' statement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 714(5) the statement is in the form and contains the information the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF statement's `s 714(5) the statement is in the prescribed form` AND statement's `s 714(5) the statement contains the prescribed information with respect to the nature of the company's business`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The directors' statement must be in the prescribed form and must contain such information with respect to the nature of the company's business as may be prescribed." (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)

-- src:9376 | (6) It must in addition have annexed to it a report addressed to the directors by the company's auditor stating that—
-- src:9377 | (a) he has inquired into the company's state of affairs,
-- src:9378 | (b) the amount specified in the statement as the permissible capital payment for the shares in question is in his view properly determined in accordance with sections 710 to 712, and
-- src:9379 | (c) he is not aware of anything to indicate that the opinion expressed by the directors in their statement as to any of the matters mentioned in subsection (3) above is unreasonable in all the circumstances.
@ref s 714(6) The statement must have annexed to it a report by the auditor stating three things (src:9376-9379)
GIVEN statement IS A `s 714(1) directors' statement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 714(6) the statement has annexed to it the report the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF statement's `s 714(6) a report addressed to the directors by the company's auditor is annexed to the statement`
       AND statement's `s 714(6)(a) the report states that the auditor has inquired into the company's state of affairs`
       AND statement's `s 714(6)(b) the report states that the amount specified as the permissible capital payment is in his view properly determined in accordance with sections 710 to 712`
       AND statement's `s 714(6)(c) the report states that he is not aware of anything to indicate that the opinion expressed by the directors as to any of the matters mentioned in subsection (3) is unreasonable in all the circumstances`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It must in addition have annexed to it a report addressed to the directors by the company's auditor stating that— (a) ..., (b) ..., and (c) ..." (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)

-- src:9366 | (1) The company's directors must make a statement in accordance with this section.
-- src:9367 | (2) The statement must specify the amount of the permissible capital payment for the shares in question.
-- src:9368 | (3) It must state that, having made full inquiry into the affairs and prospects of the company, the directors have formed the opinion—
-- src:9369 | (a) as regards its initial situation immediately following the date on which the payment out of capital is proposed to be made, that there will be no grounds on which the company could then be found unable to pay its debts, and
-- src:9370 | (b) as regards its prospects for the year immediately following that date, that having regard to—
-- src:9371 | (i) their intentions with respect to the management of the company's business during that year, and
-- src:9372 | (ii) the amount and character of the financial resources that will in their view be available to the company during that year,
-- src:9373 | the company will be able to continue to carry on business as a going concern (and will accordingly be able to pay its debts as they fall due) throughout that year.
-- src:9374 | (4) In forming their opinion for the purposes of subsection (3)(a), the directors must take into account all of the company's liabilities (including any contingent or prospective liabilities).
-- src:9375 | (5) The directors' statement must be in the prescribed form and must contain such information with respect to the nature of the company's business as may be prescribed.
-- src:9376 | (6) It must in addition have annexed to it a report addressed to the directors by the company's auditor stating that—
-- src:9377 | (a) he has inquired into the company's state of affairs,
-- src:9378 | (b) the amount specified in the statement as the permissible capital payment for the shares in question is in his view properly determined in accordance with sections 710 to 712, and
-- src:9379 | (c) he is not aware of anything to indicate that the opinion expressed by the directors in their statement as to any of the matters mentioned in subsection (3) above is unreasonable in all the circumstances.
@ref s 714(2) to (6) The statement must specify the amount, state the opinion, take account of liabilities, be in the form and carry the report (src:9366-9379)
GIVEN statement IS A `s 714(1) directors' statement`
      `the permissible capital payment, as section 710 works it out` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 714 the statement and report contain everything section 714 requires` MEANS
    IF (`s 714(2) the statement specifies the amount of the permissible capital payment` statement `the permissible capital payment, as section 710 works it out` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       AND (`s 714(3) the statement states what the subsection requires` statement EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       AND (`s 714(4) the directors took into account the liabilities the subsection requires` statement EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       AND (`s 714(5) the statement is in the form and contains the information the subsection requires` statement EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       AND (`s 714(6) the statement has annexed to it the report the subsection requires` statement EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF (`s 714(2) the statement specifies the amount of the permissible capital payment` statement `the permissible capital payment, as section 710 works it out` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
            OR (`s 714(3) the statement states what the subsection requires` statement EQUALS JUST FALSE)
            OR (`s 714(4) the directors took into account the liabilities the subsection requires` statement EQUALS JUST FALSE)
            OR (`s 714(5) the statement is in the form and contains the information the subsection requires` statement EQUALS JUST FALSE)
            OR (`s 714(6) the statement has annexed to it the report the subsection requires` statement EQUALS JUST FALSE)
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The statement must ..."; "It must state ..."; "the directors must take into account ..."; "must be in the prescribed form ..."; "It must in addition have annexed to it ..." (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a requirement of subsection (2) to (6) is not known

-- src:9366 | (1) The company's directors must make a statement in accordance with this section.
@ref s 714(1) The company's directors must make a statement in accordance with this section (src:9366-9366)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 714(1) act in Chapter 5`
`s 714(1) the directors must make a statement` MEANS
    PARTY Director
    MUST `s 714(1) make a statement in accordance with section 714`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director BECAUSE "s 714(1): the directors did not make a statement in accordance with section 714"

-- ---- s 715: offence ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9381 | (1) If the directors make a statement under section 714 without having reasonable grounds for the opinion expressed in it, an offence is committed by every director who is in default.
@ref s 715(1) Offence (src:9381-9381)
GIVEN `the directors make a statement under section 714 without having reasonable grounds for the opinion expressed in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 658(2) person charged`
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715(1) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    -- fork F-not-in-default: an officer who is not in default is answered NOTHING (the text charges only officers in default); the other reading answers JUST FALSE
    IF (NOT `the directors make a statement under section 714 without having reasonable grounds for the opinion expressed in it`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the directors make a statement under section 714 without having reasonable grounds for the opinion expressed in it"
    ELSE CONSIDER person
         WHEN `s 658(2) the company` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text charges every director who is in default
         WHEN `s 658(2) an officer of the company` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text charges every director who is in default
         WHEN `s 658(2) a director of the company` THEN
              CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who is in default"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is in default is s 1121 (coa24)
         OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text charges every director who is in default

-- src:9382 | (2) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:9383 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine (or both);
-- src:9384 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:9385 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding twelve months or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both);
-- src:9386 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both).
@ref s 715(2) Penalty (src:9382-9386)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 715(2) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    -- Penalty OF  how convicted,  imprisonment not exceeding,  fine not exceeding,  daily default fine,  imprisonment and fine together
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN
         JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, JUST (Period OF 2, Years), JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN
         JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, JUST (Period OF 12, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN
         JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, JUST (Period OF 6, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN
         JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, JUST (Period OF 6, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text gives the penalty on indictment and on summary conviction by place; a summary conviction with no place named is not a case it states

-- ---- s 716: payment to be approved by special resolution --------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9388 | (1) The payment out of capital must be approved by a special resolution of the company.
