GIVEN `the payment was approved by a resolution of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 283 the resolution is a special resolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 716(1) the payment is approved as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the payment was approved by a resolution of the company`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The payment out of capital must be approved by a special resolution of the company." (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 283 the resolution is a special resolution`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be approved by a special resolution of the company"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the resolution is a special resolution is s 283 (coa7), answered by the caller

-- src:9389 | (2) The resolution must be passed on, or within the week immediately following, the date on which the directors make the statement required by section 714.
@ref s 716(2) The resolution must be passed on, or within the week immediately following, the date on which the directors make the statement (src:9389-9389)
GIVEN `the date on which the directors make the statement` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 716(2) the last day for passing the resolution` MEANS `the date on which the directors make the statement` PLUS 7

@ref s 716(2) The resolution must be passed on, or within the week immediately following, the date on which the directors make the statement (src:9389-9389)
GIVEN `the date on which the directors make the statement` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the resolution was passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 716(2) the resolution was passed in time` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the resolution was passed` AT LEAST `the date on which the directors make the statement`
       AND `the date on which the resolution was passed` AT MOST (`s 716(2) the last day for passing the resolution` `the date on which the directors make the statement`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The resolution must be passed on, or within the week immediately following, the date on which the directors make the statement required by section 714."

-- src:9390 | (3) A resolution under this section is subject to—
-- src:9391 | section 717 (exercise of voting rights), and
-- src:9392 | section 718 (disclosure of directors' statement and auditors' report).
@ref s 716(3) A resolution under this section is subject to sections 717 and 718 (src:9390-9392)
GIVEN `s 717(3) the resolution is not effective` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 718(3) the resolution is ineffective` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 716(3) the resolution is barred by section 717 or section 718` MEANS
    IF (`s 717(3) the resolution is not effective` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`s 718(3) the resolution is ineffective` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF (`s 717(3) the resolution is not effective` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`s 718(3) the resolution is ineffective` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A resolution under this section is subject to section 717 (exercise of voting rights), and section 718 (disclosure of directors' statement and auditors' report)": neither bar bites
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 717 or 718 bars the resolution is not known

