-- src:9424 | the company must deliver to the registrar a copy of the directors' statement and auditor's report required by section 714.
@ref s 719(4) Not later than the day on which the company first publishes the notice under subsection (1), or if earlier first publishes or gives the notice under subsection (2), it must deliver to the registrar a copy of the directors' statement and auditor's report (src:9421-9424)
GIVEN `the day on which the company first publishes the notice required by subsection (1)` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the company first publishes or gives the notice required by subsection (2)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 719(4) the last day for delivering the copy to the registrar` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the company first publishes or gives the notice required by subsection (2)` LESS THAN `the day on which the company first publishes the notice required by subsection (1)`
    THEN `the day on which the company first publishes or gives the notice required by subsection (2)`
    ELSE `the day on which the company first publishes the notice required by subsection (1)`

@ref s 719(4) Not later than the day on which the company first publishes the notice under subsection (1), or if earlier first publishes or gives the notice under subsection (2), it must deliver to the registrar a copy of the directors' statement and auditor's report (src:9421-9424)
GIVEN `the day on which the company first publishes the notice required by subsection (1)` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the company first publishes or gives the notice required by subsection (2)` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the company delivered the copy to the registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 719(4) the copy was delivered to the registrar in time` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the company delivered the copy to the registrar`
         AT MOST (`s 719(4) the last day for delivering the copy to the registrar` `the day on which the company first publishes the notice required by subsection (1)` `the day on which the company first publishes or gives the notice required by subsection (2)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Not later than the day on which the company— (a) first publishes the notice required by subsection (1), or (b) if earlier, first publishes or gives the notice required by subsection (2), the company must deliver to the registrar a copy of the directors' statement and auditor's report"

@ref s 719(4) Not later than the day on which the company first publishes the notice under subsection (1), or if earlier first publishes or gives the notice under subsection (2), it must deliver to the registrar a copy of the directors' statement and auditor's report (src:9421-9424)
GIVEN `the day on which the company is to publish the notice required by subsection (1)` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the company first publishes or gives the notice required by subsection (2)` IS A DATE
      `the date of the resolution under section 716` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 714(1) act in Chapter 5`
`s 719(4) the company must deliver a copy of the statement and report to the registrar` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 719(4) deliver to the registrar a copy of the directors' statement and auditor's report`
    WITHIN (Day (`s 719(4) the last day for delivering the copy to the registrar` `the day on which the company is to publish the notice required by subsection (1)` `the day on which the company first publishes or gives the notice required by subsection (2)`) MINUS Day `the date of the resolution under section 716`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 719(4): a copy of the directors' statement and auditor's report was not delivered to the registrar by the day the company first published or gave notice"

-- ---- s 720: directors' statement and auditor's report to be available for inspection -------------------------------------------------

-- src:9426 | (1) The directors' statement and auditor's report must be kept available for inspection throughout the period—
-- src:9427 | (a) beginning with the day on which the company—
-- src:9428 | (i) first publishes the notice required by section 719(1), or
-- src:9429 | (ii) if earlier, first publishes or gives the notice required by section 719(2), and
-- src:9430 | (b) ending five weeks after the date of the resolution for payment out of capital.
@ref s 720(1) The directors' statement and auditor's report must be kept available for inspection from the first publication or giving of notice until five weeks after the date of the resolution (src:9426-9430)
GIVEN `the day on which the company first publishes the notice required by section 719(1)` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the company first publishes or gives the notice required by section 719(2)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 720(1) the first day of the period` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the company first publishes or gives the notice required by section 719(2)` LESS THAN `the day on which the company first publishes the notice required by section 719(1)`
    THEN `the day on which the company first publishes or gives the notice required by section 719(2)`
    ELSE `the day on which the company first publishes the notice required by section 719(1)`

@ref s 720(1) The directors' statement and auditor's report must be kept available for inspection throughout the period ending five weeks after the date of the resolution (src:9426-9430)
GIVEN `the date of the resolution for payment out of capital` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 720(1) the last day of the period` MEANS `the date of the resolution for payment out of capital` PLUS 35

@ref s 720(1) The directors' statement and auditor's report must be kept available for inspection throughout the period (src:9426-9430)
GIVEN `they were kept available for inspection on every day from the first day they were kept available to the last day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day on which they were kept available for inspection` IS A DATE
      `the last day on which they were kept available for inspection` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the period` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 720(1) the statement and report were kept available throughout the period` MEANS
    IF `they were kept available for inspection on every day from the first day they were kept available to the last day`
       AND `the first day on which they were kept available for inspection` AT MOST `the first day of the period`
       AND `the last day on which they were kept available for inspection` AT LEAST `the last day of the period`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be kept available for inspection throughout the period— (a) beginning with the day on which the company ... first publishes the notice ..., and (b) ending five weeks after the date of the resolution for payment out of capital" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)

-- src:9431 | (2) They must be kept available for inspection—
-- src:9432 | (a) at the company's registered office, or
-- src:9433 | (b) at a place specified in regulations under section 1136.
@ref s 720(2) They must be kept available at the registered office or at a place specified in regulations under section 1136 (src:9431-9433)
GIVEN `they are kept at the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are kept at a place specified in regulations under section 1136` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 720(2) the statement and report are kept at a place the subsection allows` MEANS
    IF `they are kept at the company's registered office` OR `they are kept at a place specified in regulations under section 1136`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "They must be kept available for inspection— (a) at the company's registered office, or (b) at a place specified in regulations under section 1136." (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)

-- src:9434 | (3) The company must give notice to the registrar—
-- src:9435 | (a) of the place at which the statement and report are kept available for inspection, and
-- src:9436 | (b) of any change in that place,
-- src:9437 | unless they have at all times been kept at the company's registered office.
@ref s 720(3) The company must give notice to the registrar of the place and of any change, unless they have at all times been kept at the registered office (src:9434-9437)
GIVEN `they have at all times been kept at the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 720(3) the company must give notice to the registrar of the place` MEANS
    IF `they have at all times been kept at the company's registered office`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless they have at all times been kept at the company's registered office"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 720(3) The company must give notice to the registrar of the place and of any change (src:9434-9437)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 714(1) act in Chapter 5`
`s 720(3) the company's duty to give notice to the registrar of the place` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 720(3) give notice to the registrar of the place at which the statement and report are kept available for inspection and of any change in that place`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 720(3): the company did not give notice to the registrar of the place at which the statement and report are kept"

DECLARE `s 720(4) who inspects` IS ONE OF
    `s 720(4) a member of the company`
    `s 720(4) a creditor of the company`
    `s 720(4) any other person`

-- src:9438 | (4) They must be open to the inspection of any member or creditor of the company without charge.
@ref s 720(4) They must be open to the inspection of any member or creditor of the company without charge (src:9438-9438)
GIVEN who IS A `s 720(4) who inspects`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 720(4) the person may inspect the statement and report without charge` MEANS
    CONSIDER who
    WHEN `s 720(4) any other person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any member or creditor of the company"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:9439 | (5) If default is made for 14 days in complying with subsection (3), or an inspection under subsection (4) is refused, an offence is committed by—
-- src:9440 | (a) the company, and
-- src:9441 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 720(5) Default for 14 days in complying with subsection (3), or a refusal of an inspection under subsection (4) (src:9439-9441)
GIVEN `the number of days for which default has been made in complying with subsection (3)` IS A NUMBER
      `an inspection under subsection (4) is refused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 720(5) the company is in default as the subsection describes` MEANS
    IF `the number of days for which default has been made in complying with subsection (3)` AT LEAST 14 OR `an inspection under subsection (4) is refused`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made for 14 days in complying with subsection (3), or an inspection under subsection (4) is refused"

-- src:9439 | (5) If default is made for 14 days in complying with subsection (3), or an inspection under subsection (4) is refused, an offence is committed by—
-- src:9440 | (a) the company, and
-- src:9441 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 720(5) Offence (src:9439-9441)
GIVEN `the company is in default as section 720(5) describes` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 658(2) person charged`
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 720(5) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    -- fork F-not-in-default: an officer who is not in default is answered NOTHING (the text charges only officers in default); the other reading answers JUST FALSE
    IF (NOT `the company is in default as section 720(5) describes`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made for 14 days in complying with subsection (3), or an inspection under subsection (4) is refused"
    ELSE CONSIDER person
         WHEN `s 658(2) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 658(2) an officer of the company` THEN
              CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who is in default"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is in default is s 1121 (coa24)
         WHEN `s 658(2) a director of the company` THEN
              CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who is in default"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is in default is s 1121 (coa24)
         OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text charges the company and every officer of the company who is in default

-- src:9442 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 720(6) Penalty (src:9442-9442)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 720(6) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    -- Penalty OF  how convicted,  imprisonment not exceeding,  fine not exceeding,  daily default fine,  imprisonment and fine together
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states the penalty on summary conviction only
    OTHERWISE JUST (Penalty OF how, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE)

-- src:9443 | (7) In the case of a refusal of an inspection required by subsection (4), the court may by order compel an immediate inspection.
@ref s 720(7) In the case of a refusal of an inspection required by subsection (4), the court may by order compel an immediate inspection (src:9443-9443)
GIVEN `an inspection under subsection (4) is refused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 720(7) the court may order an immediate inspection` MEANS
    IF `an inspection under subsection (4) is refused`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of a refusal of an inspection required by subsection (4), the court may by order compel an immediate inspection"

-- ---- s 720A: reduced requirements for employees' share schemes --------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9446 | (1) Section 713(1) does not apply to the purchase out of capital by a private company of its own shares for the purposes of or pursuant to an employees' share scheme when approved by special resolution supported by a solvency statement.
@ref s 720A(1) Section 713(1) does not apply to a purchase out of capital by a private company for an employees' share scheme when approved by special resolution supported by a solvency statement (src:9446-9446)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1166 the purchase is for the purposes of or pursuant to an employees' share scheme` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 283 the resolution is a special resolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 720A(2) the resolution is supported by a solvency statement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 720A(1) section 713(1) does not apply` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a private company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the purchase out of capital by a private company of its own shares"
    ELSE IF (`s 1166 the purchase is for the purposes of or pursuant to an employees' share scheme` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            AND (`s 283 the resolution is a special resolution` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            AND (`s 720A(2) the resolution is supported by a solvency statement` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF (`s 1166 the purchase is for the purposes of or pursuant to an employees' share scheme` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
                 OR (`s 283 the resolution is a special resolution` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
                 OR (`s 720A(2) the resolution is supported by a solvency statement` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 713(1) does not apply to the purchase out of capital ... for the purposes of or pursuant to an employees' share scheme when approved by special resolution supported by a solvency statement"
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the purchase is for an employees' share scheme (s 1166), the resolution is special (s 283) or a solvency statement supports it is not known

-- src:9447 | (2) For the purposes of this section a resolution is supported by a solvency statement if—
-- src:9448 | (a) the directors of the company make a solvency statement (see section 643) not more than 15 days before the date on which the resolution is passed, and
-- src:9449 | (b) the resolution and solvency statement are registered in accordance with section 720B.
@ref s 720A(2) A resolution is supported by a solvency statement if the directors make a solvency statement not more than 15 days before the resolution is passed and the resolution and statement are registered under section 720B (src:9447-9449)
GIVEN `s 643 the directors made a solvency statement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the directors made the solvency statement` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the resolution is passed` IS A DATE
      `the resolution and solvency statement are registered in accordance with section 720B` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 720A(2) the resolution is supported by a solvency statement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 643 the directors made a solvency statement`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a resolution is supported by a solvency statement if— (a) the directors of the company make a solvency statement"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the directors made a solvency statement is s 643 (coa14), answered by the caller
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
         IF `the date on which the directors made the solvency statement` AT MOST `the date on which the resolution is passed`
            AND `the date on which the directors made the solvency statement` AT LEAST (`the date on which the resolution is passed` MINUS 15)
            AND `the resolution and solvency statement are registered in accordance with section 720B`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) ... not more than 15 days before the date on which the resolution is passed, and (b) the resolution and solvency statement are registered in accordance with section 720B"

-- src:9450 | (3) Where the resolution is proposed as a written resolution, a copy of the solvency statement must be sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution is sent or submitted to the member.
@ref s 720A(3) Written resolution: a copy of the solvency statement is sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time the proposed resolution is sent (src:9450-9450)
GIVEN `the copy was sent or submitted to every eligible member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the copy was sent or submitted` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the proposed resolution was sent or submitted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 720A(3) the copy of the solvency statement was sent or submitted in time` MEANS
    `s 696(2)(a) the copy or memorandum was made available to members for a written resolution` `the copy was sent or submitted to every eligible member` `the date on which the copy was sent or submitted` `the date on which the proposed resolution was sent or submitted`

-- src:9451 | (4) Where the resolution is proposed at a general meeting, a copy of the solvency statement must be made available for inspection by members of the company throughout that meeting.
@ref s 720A(4) General meeting: a copy of the solvency statement is made available for inspection by members throughout the meeting (src:9451-9451)
GIVEN `a copy of the solvency statement was made available for inspection by members of the company throughout the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 720A(4) the copy of the solvency statement was made available at the meeting` MEANS
    IF `a copy of the solvency statement was made available for inspection by members of the company throughout the meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the resolution is proposed at a general meeting, a copy of the solvency statement must be made available for inspection by members of the company throughout that meeting." (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)

-- src:9452 | (5) The validity of a resolution is not affected by a failure to comply with subsection (3) or (4).
@ref s 720A(5) The validity of a resolution is not affected by a failure to comply with subsection (3) or (4) (src:9452-9452)
GIVEN `there is a failure to comply with subsection (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 720A(5) the validity of the resolution is affected by the failure` MEANS
    IF `there is a failure to comply with subsection (3) or (4)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The validity of a resolution is not affected by a failure to comply with subsection (3) or (4)."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a failure to comply with subsection (3) or (4)"

-- src:9453 | (6) Section 717 (resolution authorising payment: exercise of voting rights) applies to a resolution under this section as it applies to a resolution under section 716.
@ref s 720A(6) Section 717 applies to a resolution under this section as it applies to a resolution under section 716 (src:9453-9453)
GIVEN `the resolution is a resolution under section 720A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 720A(6) section 717 applies to the resolution` MEANS
    IF `the resolution is a resolution under section 720A`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "applies to a resolution under this section"

-- ---- s 720B: registration of resolution and supporting documents --------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9455 | (1) Within 15 days after the passing of the resolution for a payment out of capital by a private company for the purchase of its own shares for the purposes of or pursuant to an employees' share scheme the company must deliver to the registrar–
-- src:9456 | (a) a copy of the solvency statement,
-- src:9457 | (b) a copy of the resolution, and
-- src:9458 | (c) a statement of capital.
@ref s 720B(1) Within 15 days after the passing of the resolution the company must deliver to the registrar a copy of the solvency statement, a copy of the resolution and a statement of capital (src:9455-9458)
GIVEN `the date on which the resolution was passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 720B(1) the last day for delivering the documents to the registrar` MEANS `the date on which the resolution was passed` PLUS 15

@ref s 720B(1) Within 15 days after the passing of the resolution the company must deliver to the registrar a copy of the solvency statement, a copy of the resolution and a statement of capital (src:9455-9458)
GIVEN `the date on which the resolution was passed` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the company delivered the documents to the registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 720B(1) the documents were delivered within 15 days after the resolution was passed` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the company delivered the documents to the registrar` AT LEAST `the date on which the resolution was passed`
       AND `the date on which the company delivered the documents to the registrar` AT MOST (`s 720B(1) the last day for delivering the documents to the registrar` `the date on which the resolution was passed`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Within 15 days after the passing of the resolution ... the company must deliver to the registrar"

@ref s 720B(1) Within 15 days after the passing of the resolution the company must deliver to the registrar a copy of the solvency statement, a copy of the resolution and a statement of capital (src:9455-9458)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 714(1) act in Chapter 5`
`s 720B(1) the company must deliver the documents to the registrar` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 720B(1) deliver to the registrar a copy of the solvency statement, a copy of the resolution and a statement of capital`
    WITHIN 15
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 720B(1): the documents were not delivered to the registrar within 15 days after the resolution was passed"

-- src:9459 | (2) The statement of capital must state with respect to the company's share capital as reduced by the resolution—
-- src:9460 | (a) the total number of shares of the company,
-- src:9461 | (b) the aggregate nominal value of those shares,
-- src:9462 | (ba) the aggregate amount (if any) unpaid on those shares (whether on account of their nominal value or by way of premium), and
-- src:9463 | (c) for each class of shares—
-- src:9464 | (i) prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares,
-- src:9465 | (ii) the total number of shares of that class, and
-- src:9466 | (iii) the aggregate nominal value of shares of that class, ...
-- src:9467 | (d) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
@ref s 720B(2) The statement of capital must state the same five things as in section 663(3), for the share capital as reduced by the resolution (src:9459-9467)
GIVEN statement IS A `s 663(3) statement of capital`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 720B(2) the statement of capital states what the subsection requires` MEANS
    -- the same words as s 663(3), with respect to the share capital as reduced by the resolution; the helper of s 663(3) answers
    `s 663(3) the statement of capital states what the section requires` statement

-- src:9468 | (3) The registrar must register the documents delivered to him under subsection (1) on receipt.
@ref s 720B(3) The registrar must register the documents delivered under subsection (1) on receipt (src:9468-9468)
GIVEN `the documents were delivered to the registrar under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 720B(3) the registrar must register the documents on receipt` MEANS
    IF `the documents were delivered to the registrar under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the documents delivered to him under subsection (1)"

@ref s 720B(3) The registrar must register the documents delivered under subsection (1) on receipt (src:9468-9468)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 714(1) act in Chapter 5`
`s 720B(3) the registrar must register the documents` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 720B(3) register the documents delivered to him`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "s 720B(3): the registrar did not register the documents on receipt"

-- src:9469 | (4) The resolution does not take effect until those documents are registered.
@ref s 720B(4) The resolution does not take effect until those documents are registered (src:9469-9469)
GIVEN `the documents delivered under subsection (1) have been registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 720B(4) the resolution cannot yet take effect` MEANS
    IF `the documents delivered under subsection (1) have been registered`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The resolution does not take effect until those documents are registered": the bar lifts on registration
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:9470 | (5) The company must also deliver to the registrar, within 15 days after the resolution is passed, a statement by the directors confirming that the solvency statement was—
-- src:9471 | (a) made not more than 15 days before the date on which the resolution was passed, and
-- src:9472 | (b) provided to members in accordance with section 720A(3) or (4).
@ref s 720B(5) The company must also deliver to the registrar, within 15 days after the resolution is passed, a statement by the directors confirming the solvency statement (src:9470-9472)
GIVEN `the date on which the resolution was passed` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the company delivered the directors' statement to the registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 720B(5) the directors' statement was delivered within 15 days after the resolution was passed` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the company delivered the directors' statement to the registrar` AT LEAST `the date on which the resolution was passed`
       AND `the date on which the company delivered the directors' statement to the registrar` AT MOST (`s 720B(1) the last day for delivering the documents to the registrar` `the date on which the resolution was passed`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company must also deliver to the registrar, within 15 days after the resolution is passed, a statement by the directors"

@ref s 720B(5) The company must also deliver to the registrar, within 15 days after the resolution is passed, a statement by the directors confirming the solvency statement (src:9470-9472)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 714(1) act in Chapter 5`
`s 720B(5) the company must deliver the directors' statement to the registrar` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 720B(5) deliver to the registrar a statement by the directors confirming the solvency statement`
    WITHIN 15
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 720B(5): the directors' statement was not delivered to the registrar within 15 days after the resolution was passed"

@ref s 720B(5) The statement must confirm that the solvency statement was made not more than 15 days before the resolution and provided to members under section 720A(3) or (4) (src:9470-9472)
GIVEN `the statement confirms that the solvency statement was made not more than 15 days before the date on which the resolution was passed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement confirms that the solvency statement was provided to members in accordance with section 720A(3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 720B(5) the statement confirms what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the statement confirms that the solvency statement was made not more than 15 days before the date on which the resolution was passed`
       AND `the statement confirms that the solvency statement was provided to members in accordance with section 720A(3) or (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a statement by the directors confirming that the solvency statement was— (a) made not more than 15 days before the date on which the resolution was passed, and (b) provided to members in accordance with section 720A(3) or (4)" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)

-- src:9473 | (6) The validity of a resolution is not affected by—
-- src:9474 | (a) a failure to deliver the documents required to be delivered to the registrar under subsection (1) within the time specified in that subsection, or
-- src:9475 | (b) a failure to comply with subsection (5).
@ref s 720B(6) The validity of a resolution is not affected by a late delivery under subsection (1) or a failure to comply with subsection (5) (src:9473-9475)
GIVEN `the documents were not delivered within the time specified in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a failure to comply with subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 720B(6) the validity of the resolution is affected by the failure` MEANS
    IF `the documents were not delivered within the time specified in subsection (1)` OR `there is a failure to comply with subsection (5)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The validity of a resolution is not affected by— (a) a failure to deliver the documents ... within the time specified in that subsection, or (b) a failure to comply with subsection (5)"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a failure to deliver the documents ... within the time specified in that subsection, or ... a failure to comply with subsection (5)"

-- src:9476 | (7) If the company delivers to the registrar a solvency statement that was not provided to members in accordance with section 720A(3) or (4), an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 720B(7) Offence (src:9476-9476)
GIVEN `the company delivers to the registrar a solvency statement that was not provided to members in accordance with section 720A(3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 658(2) person charged`
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 720B(7) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    -- fork F-not-in-default: an officer who is not in default is answered NOTHING (the text charges only officers in default); the other reading answers JUST FALSE
    IF (NOT `the company delivers to the registrar a solvency statement that was not provided to members in accordance with section 720A(3) or (4)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the company delivers to the registrar a solvency statement that was not provided to members in accordance with section 720A(3) or (4)"
    ELSE CONSIDER person
         WHEN `s 658(2) the company` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text charges every officer of the company who is in default
         WHEN `s 658(2) an officer of the company` THEN
              CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who is in default"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is in default is s 1121 (coa24)
         WHEN `s 658(2) a director of the company` THEN
              CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who is in default"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is in default is s 1121 (coa24)
         OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text charges every officer of the company who is in default

-- src:9477 | (8) If default is made in complying with this section, an offence is committed by–
-- src:9478 | (a) the company, and
-- src:9479 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 720B(8) Offence (src:9477-9479)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 720B` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 658(2) person charged`
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 720B(8) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    -- fork F-not-in-default: an officer who is not in default is answered NOTHING (the text charges only officers in default); the other reading answers JUST FALSE
    IF (NOT `default is made in complying with section 720B`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with this section"
    ELSE CONSIDER person
         WHEN `s 658(2) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 658(2) an officer of the company` THEN
              CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who is in default"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is in default is s 1121 (coa24)
         WHEN `s 658(2) a director of the company` THEN
              CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who is in default"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is in default is s 1121 (coa24)
         OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text charges the company and every officer of the company who is in default

-- src:9480 | (9) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (7) or (8) is liable–
-- src:9481 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:9482 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 720B(9) Penalty on conviction of an offence under subsection (7) or (8) (src:9480-9482)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 720B(9) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    -- Penalty OF  how convicted,  imprisonment not exceeding,  fine not exceeding,  daily default fine,  imprisonment and fine together
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)

-- ---- s 721: application to court to cancel resolution --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 721(1) who applies` IS ONE OF
    `s 721(1)(a) a member of the company` HAS `s 721(1)(a) he consented to or voted in favour of the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 721(1)(b) a creditor of the company`
    `s 721(1) any other person`

-- src:9485 | (1) Where a private company passes a special resolution approving a payment out of capital for the redemption or purchase of any of its shares—
-- src:9486 | (a) any member of the company (other than one who consented to or voted in favour of the resolution), and
-- src:9487 | (b) any creditor of the company,
-- src:9488 | may apply to the court for the cancellation of the resolution.
@ref s 721(1) Where a private company passes a special resolution approving a payment out of capital, any member (other than one who consented or voted in favour) and any creditor may apply to the court for its cancellation (src:9485-9488)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 283 the resolution is a special resolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the resolution approves a payment out of capital for the redemption or purchase of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      applicant IS A `s 721(1) who applies`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 721(1) the person may apply to the court for the cancellation of the resolution` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a private company`) OR (NOT `the resolution approves a payment out of capital for the redemption or purchase of shares`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a private company passes a special resolution approving a payment out of capital for the redemption or purchase of any of its shares"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 283 the resolution is a special resolution`
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a private company passes a special resolution approving a payment out of capital"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the resolution is a special resolution is s 283 (coa7), answered by the caller
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
              CONSIDER applicant
              WHEN `s 721(1)(a) a member of the company` consented THEN
                   IF consented
                   THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(other than one who consented to or voted in favour of the resolution)"
                   ELSE JUST TRUE
              WHEN `s 721(1)(b) a creditor of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `s 721(1) any other person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) any member of the company ..., and (b) any creditor of the company, may apply to the court"

@ref s 721(1) Any member (other than one who consented or voted in favour) and any creditor may apply to the court for the cancellation of the resolution (src:9485-9488)
GIVEN who IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 714(1) act in Chapter 5`
`s 721(1) the member or creditor may apply to the court` MEANS
    PARTY who
    MAY `s 721(1) apply to the court for the cancellation of the resolution`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:9490 | (a) must be made within five weeks after the passing of the resolution, and
@ref s 721(2)(a) The application must be made within five weeks after the passing of the resolution (src:9490-9490)
GIVEN `the date on which the resolution was passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 721(2)(a) the last day for applying to the court` MEANS `the date on which the resolution was passed` PLUS 35

@ref s 721(2)(a) The application must be made within five weeks after the passing of the resolution (src:9490-9490)
GIVEN `the date on which the resolution was passed` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the application was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 721(2)(a) the application was made within five weeks after the passing of the resolution` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the application was made` AT LEAST `the date on which the resolution was passed`
       AND `the date on which the application was made` AT MOST (`s 721(2)(a) the last day for applying to the court` `the date on which the resolution was passed`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The application— (a) must be made within five weeks after the passing of the resolution"

-- src:9491 | (b) may be made on behalf of the persons entitled to make it by such one or more of their number as they may appoint in writing for the purpose.
@ref s 721(2)(b) The application may be made on behalf of the persons entitled by one or more of their number appointed in writing (src:9491-9491)
GIVEN `the person is one or more of the persons entitled to make the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he has been appointed in writing by those persons for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 721(2)(b) the application may be made on behalf of the persons entitled by the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is one or more of the persons entitled to make the application` AND `he has been appointed in writing by those persons for the purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on behalf of the persons entitled to make it by such one or more of their number as they may appoint in writing for the purpose"

-- src:9492 | (3) On an application under this section the court may if it thinks fit—
-- src:9493 | (a) adjourn the proceedings in order that an arrangement may be made to the satisfaction of the court—
-- src:9494 | (i) for the purchase of the interests of dissentient members, or
-- src:9495 | (ii) for the protection of dissentient creditors, and
-- src:9496 | (b) give such directions and make such orders as it thinks expedient for facilitating or carrying into effect any such arrangement.
@ref s 721(3) On an application the court may if it thinks fit adjourn the proceedings for an arrangement and give directions (src:9492-9496)
GIVEN `an application has been made under section 721` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 721(3) the court may adjourn the proceedings and give directions and make orders` MEANS
    IF `an application has been made under section 721` AND `the court thinks fit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On an application under this section the court may if it thinks fit—"

DECLARE `s 721(4) order` IS ONE OF
    `s 721(4) an order cancelling the resolution`
    `s 721(4) an order confirming the resolution`
    `s 721(4) any other order`

-- src:9497 | (4) Subject to that, the court must make an order either cancelling or confirming the resolution, and may do so on such terms and conditions as it thinks fit.
@ref s 721(4) The court must make an order either cancelling or confirming the resolution (src:9497-9497)
GIVEN `the court has made an order under section 721` IS A BOOLEAN
      order IS A `s 721(4) order`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 721(4) the court has made the order the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the court has made an order under section 721`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to that, the court must make an order either cancelling or confirming the resolution" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-must)
    ELSE CONSIDER order
         WHEN `s 721(4) any other order` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an order either cancelling or confirming the resolution": subsections (3), (6) and (7) allow other orders
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 721(4) The court must make an order either cancelling or confirming the resolution (src:9497-9497)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 714(1) act in Chapter 5`
`s 721(4) the court must make an order cancelling or confirming the resolution` MEANS
    PARTY Court
    MUST `s 721(4) make an order either cancelling or confirming the resolution`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Court BECAUSE "s 721(4): the court did not make an order either cancelling or confirming the resolution"

-- src:9498 | (5) If the court confirms the resolution, it may by order alter or extend any date or period of time specified—
-- src:9499 | (a) in the resolution, or
-- src:9500 | (b) in any provision of this Chapter applying to the redemption or purchase to which the resolution relates.
@ref s 721(5) If the court confirms the resolution, it may by order alter or extend any date or period of time specified in the resolution or in a provision of this Chapter (src:9498-9500)
GIVEN `the court confirms the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date or period is specified in the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date or period is specified in a provision of this Chapter applying to the redemption or purchase to which the resolution relates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 721(5) the court may by order alter or extend the date or period` MEANS
    -- fork F-grant-721-5: "If the court confirms the resolution, it may by order alter or extend" is a grant or a power; where its gate fails the answer is NOTHING; the other reading answers JUST FALSE (a failed "if" read as the text's own no)
    IF (NOT `the court confirms the resolution`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the court confirms the resolution, it may by order alter or extend"
    ELSE IF `the date or period is specified in the resolution` OR `the date or period is specified in a provision of this Chapter applying to the redemption or purchase to which the resolution relates`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any date or period of time specified— (a) in the resolution, or (b) in any provision of this Chapter applying to the redemption or purchase"

-- src:9501 | (6) The court's order may, if the court thinks fit—
-- src:9502 | (a) provide for the purchase by the company of the shares of any of its members and for the reduction accordingly of the company's capital, and
-- src:9503 | (b) make any alteration in the company's articles that may be required in consequence of that provision.
@ref s 721(6) The court's order may, if the court thinks fit, provide for the purchase by the company of the shares of any of its members and alter the articles (src:9501-9503)
GIVEN `the court thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 721(6) the court's order may provide for the purchase of a member's shares and alter the articles` MEANS
    -- fork F-grant-721-6: "The court's order may, if the court thinks fit" is a grant or a power; where its gate fails the answer is NOTHING; the other reading answers JUST FALSE (a failed "if" read as the text's own no)
    IF `the court thinks fit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court's order may, if the court thinks fit"

-- src:9504 | (7) The court's order may, if the court thinks fit, require the company not to make any, or any specified, amendments of its articles without the leave of the court.
@ref s 721(7) The court's order may, if the court thinks fit, require the company not to make amendments of its articles without the leave of the court (src:9504-9504)
GIVEN `the court thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 721(7) the court's order may restrict amendments of the articles` MEANS
    -- fork F-grant-721-7: "The court's order may, if the court thinks fit" is a grant or a power; where its gate fails the answer is NOTHING; the other reading answers JUST FALSE (a failed "if" read as the text's own no)
    IF `the court thinks fit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court's order may, if the court thinks fit, require the company not to make any, or any specified, amendments of its articles without the leave of the court"

-- ---- s 722: notice to registrar of court application or order ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- "immediately" is read as on the day of the event (clock day 0): see F-immediately in NOTES.md.
-- src:9506 | (1) On making an application under section 721 (application to court to cancel resolution) the applicants, or the person making the application on their behalf, must immediately give notice to the registrar.
-- src:9507 | This is without prejudice to any provision of rules of court as to service of notice of the application.
@ref s 722(1) On making an application under section 721 the applicants must immediately give notice to the registrar (src:9506-9507)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 714(1) act in Chapter 5`
`s 722(1) the applicants must give notice to the registrar` MEANS
    -- fork F-immediately: "immediately" is read as on the day of the event (clock day 0); the other reading allows a short time after it
    PARTY Member
    MUST `s 722(1) give notice to the registrar of the application`
    WITHIN 0
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Member BECAUSE "s 722(1): the applicants did not immediately give notice to the registrar of the application"

-- src:9508 | (2) On being served with notice of any such application, the company must immediately give notice to the registrar.
@ref s 722(2) On being served with notice of the application, the company must immediately give notice to the registrar (src:9508-9508)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 714(1) act in Chapter 5`
`s 722(2) the company must give notice to the registrar` MEANS
    -- fork F-immediately: "immediately" is read as on the day of the event (clock day 0); the other reading allows a short time after it
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 722(2) give notice to the registrar of the notice of the application`
    WITHIN 0
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 722(2): the company did not immediately give notice to the registrar"

-- src:9509 | (3) Within 15 days of the making of the court's order on the application, or such longer period as the court may at any time direct, the company must deliver to the registrar a copy of the order.
@ref s 722(3) Within 15 days of the making of the court's order, or such longer period as the court may direct, the company must deliver to the registrar a copy of the order (src:9509-9509)
GIVEN `the date on which the court made the order` IS A DATE
      `the period longer than 15 days that the court has directed, in days, if it has` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 722(3) the last day for delivering a copy of the order to the registrar` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the period longer than 15 days that the court has directed, in days, if it has`
    WHEN JUST n THEN IF n GREATER THAN 15 THEN `the date on which the court made the order` PLUS n ELSE `the date on which the court made the order` PLUS 15
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the date on which the court made the order` PLUS 15

@ref s 722(3) Within 15 days of the making of the court's order, or such longer period as the court may direct, the company must deliver to the registrar a copy of the order (src:9509-9509)
GIVEN `the date on which the court made the order` IS A DATE
      `the period longer than 15 days that the court has directed, in days, if it has` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the date on which the company delivered a copy of the order to the registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 722(3) the copy of the order was delivered in time` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the company delivered a copy of the order to the registrar` AT LEAST `the date on which the court made the order`
       AND `the date on which the company delivered a copy of the order to the registrar`
             AT MOST (`s 722(3) the last day for delivering a copy of the order to the registrar` `the date on which the court made the order` `the period longer than 15 days that the court has directed, in days, if it has`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Within 15 days of the making of the court's order, or such longer period as the court may at any time direct, the company must deliver to the registrar a copy of the order"

@ref s 722(3) Within 15 days of the making of the court's order, or such longer period as the court may direct, the company must deliver to the registrar a copy of the order (src:9509-9509)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 714(1) act in Chapter 5`
`s 722(3) the company must deliver a copy of the order to the registrar` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 722(3) deliver to the registrar a copy of the court's order`
    WITHIN 15
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 722(3): a copy of the court's order was not delivered to the registrar within 15 days of the making of the order"

-- src:9510 | (4) If a company fails to comply with subsection (2) or (3) an offence is committed by—
-- src:9511 | (a) the company, and
-- src:9512 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 722(4) Offence (src:9510-9512)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with subsection (2) or (3) of section 722` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 658(2) person charged`
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 722(4) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    -- fork F-not-in-default: an officer who is not in default is answered NOTHING (the text charges only officers in default); the other reading answers JUST FALSE
    IF (NOT `the company fails to comply with subsection (2) or (3) of section 722`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with subsection (2) or (3)"
    ELSE CONSIDER person
         WHEN `s 658(2) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 658(2) an officer of the company` THEN
              CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who is in default"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is in default is s 1121 (coa24)
         WHEN `s 658(2) a director of the company` THEN
              CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who is in default"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is in default is s 1121 (coa24)
         OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text charges the company and every officer of the company who is in default

-- src:9513 | (5) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 722(5) Penalty (src:9513-9513)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 722(5) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    -- Penalty OF  how convicted,  imprisonment not exceeding,  fine not exceeding,  daily default fine,  imprisonment and fine together
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states the penalty on summary conviction only
    OTHERWISE JUST (Penalty OF how, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE)

-- ---- s 723: time when payment out of capital to be made or shares to be surrendered ------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9516 | (1) The payment out of capital , if made in accordance with a resolution under section 716 must be made—
-- src:9517 | (a) no earlier than five weeks after the date on which the resolution under section 716 is passed, and
-- src:9518 | (b) no more than seven weeks after that date.
@ref s 723(1) The payment out of capital must be made no earlier than five weeks, and no more than seven weeks, after the date on which the resolution is passed (src:9516-9518)
GIVEN `the date on which the resolution under section 716 was passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 723(1)(a) the first day on which the payment may be made` MEANS `the date on which the resolution under section 716 was passed` PLUS 35

@ref s 723(1) The payment out of capital must be made no earlier than five weeks, and no more than seven weeks, after the date on which the resolution is passed (src:9516-9518)
GIVEN `the date on which the resolution under section 716 was passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 723(1)(b) the last day on which the payment may be made` MEANS `the date on which the resolution under section 716 was passed` PLUS 49

@ref s 723(1) The payment out of capital must be made no earlier than five weeks, and no more than seven weeks, after the date on which the resolution is passed (src:9516-9518)
GIVEN `the date on which the resolution under section 716 was passed` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the payment out of capital was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 723(1) the payment out of capital was made in the window` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the payment out of capital was made` AT LEAST (`s 723(1)(a) the first day on which the payment may be made` `the date on which the resolution under section 716 was passed`)
       AND `the date on which the payment out of capital was made` AT MOST (`s 723(1)(b) the last day on which the payment may be made` `the date on which the resolution under section 716 was passed`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be made— (a) no earlier than five weeks after the date on which the resolution under section 716 is passed, and (b) no more than seven weeks after that date"

-- The closing edge as a regulative rule (the lower edge, day 35, is in the decision function: `AFTER` is not available on the stable binary).
@ref s 723(1) The payment out of capital must be made no earlier than five weeks, and no more than seven weeks, after the date on which the resolution is passed (src:9516-9518)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 714(1) act in Chapter 5`
`s 723(1) the company must make the payment out of capital by the closing day` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 723(1) make the payment out of capital`
    WITHIN 49
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 723(1): the payment out of capital was not made within seven weeks after the date on which the resolution was passed"

-- src:9519 | (1A) Shares to be purchased in accordance with a resolution under section 720A must be surrendered—
-- src:9520 | (a) no earlier than five weeks after the date on which the resolution under section 720A is passed, and
-- src:9521 | (b) no later than seven weeks after that date.
@ref s 723(1A) Shares to be purchased in accordance with a resolution under section 720A must be surrendered no earlier than five weeks and no later than seven weeks after the date the resolution is passed (src:9519-9521)
GIVEN `the date on which the resolution under section 720A was passed` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the shares were surrendered` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 723(1A) the shares were surrendered in the window` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the shares were surrendered` AT LEAST (`the date on which the resolution under section 720A was passed` PLUS 35)
       AND `the date on which the shares were surrendered` AT MOST (`the date on which the resolution under section 720A was passed` PLUS 49)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be surrendered— (a) no earlier than five weeks after the date on which the resolution under section 720A is passed, and (b) no later than seven weeks after that date"

-- src:9522 | (2) This is subject to any exercise of the court's powers under section 721(5) (power to alter or extend time where resolution confirmed after objection).
@ref s 723(2) This is subject to any exercise of the court's powers under section 721(5) (src:9522-9522)
GIVEN `the court has by order under section 721(5) altered or extended the date or period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 723(2) the dates and periods of subsection (1) are displaced by the court's order` MEANS
    IF `the court has by order under section 721(5) altered or extended the date or period`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This is subject to any exercise of the court's powers under section 721(5)": with no exercise the dates and periods stand
